            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0426" n="418" xml:id="pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/2043: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-29T13:00:00+01:00">December 29, 1938—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 29—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>764. 1. A German decree of December 14 published in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reichsgesetzblatt</hi> 1 of December 23 received this morning provides
                    (insofar as we are able to interpret it) for the elimination of Jews as managers
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Betriebs Führer</hi>) of plants or as acting
                    managers.</p>
                <p>2. I am sending a third-person note under today’s date to the Foreign Office
                    requesting assurances that American citizens will be exempted from its
                    application.</p>
                <p>3. I wish to add that I felt it desirable to take this position. We are, however,
                    unable to ascertain as yet whether as a practical issue American citizens are
                    actually affected.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
